### This file works with the built-in HTTP Client in WebStorm/IntelliJ
### (look for the green "run" arrow next to each request), or with the
### "REST Client" extension in VS Code.
###
### Run these top to bottom. Requests 1 and 2 save the JWT token into a
### variable called "token", which the rest of the requests reuse.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lolka23433424354543242433433123253345443423425435345432423433@example.com",
  "password": "ppsdodsadsafdsfsdfsdfdsfsdfsdgfdgfdsfssfdfdsfsgfdgdfdsfsfgsdfsdffsfdsfsdfdfsddfsdfsdfs"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### 2. Login (use this instead of #1 once the user already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lolka23433424354543242433433123253345443423425435345432423433@example.com",
  "password": "ppsdodsadsafdsfsdfsdfdsfsdfsdgfdgfdsfssfdfdsfsgfdgdfdsfsfgsdfsdffsfdsfsdfdfsddfsdfsdfs"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### 3. Create a product (needs the token from #1 or #2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": " name Ivan",
  "description": " description Ivan",
  "price" : 10345
}

### 4. Get all products for the logged-in user
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Get a single product by id (change the id to match a real one from #3/#4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Update a product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Updated name",
  "description": "Updated description",
  "price" : 20
}

### 7. Delete a product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Sanity check: same request without a token should fail with 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### 9. Create settings for user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/1/settings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "settingsName": "lolka",
  "attributes": {
    "color": "black",
    "country": "Ukraine"
  }
}
